      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt from the Suffolk Local Authorities website \u0027\u003Ca href=\u0022http://www.onesuffolk.net/\u0022\u003E1Suffolk\u003C/a\u003E\u0027;",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003ESt Edmund\u0027s Buns\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Ci\u003EIngredients\u003C/i\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; 1-and-a-half lbs flour\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; 1-and-a-half teaspoons of salt\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; 2 oz of butter\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; 2 teaspoons of mixed spice\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; 3 oz Sugar\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; 4 oz sultanas\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u00BD pint tepid milk\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; \u00BC pint of tepid water\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; 1 oz of yeast\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Ci\u003EMethod\u003C/i\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; Mix together and then place small portions of the dough onto a baking tray.\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; Allow to rise in a warm place until nearly double in size. Then bake in a preheated oven at 160 to 180 for about 25 to 30 minutes, or until brown.\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; Cover with sugar solution and enjoy! Best eaten warm.\u003Cbr\u003E"
    }
